1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:05,484
Ratios, rates, and unit conversions
look like the easy part of the SAT math

2
00:00:05,504 --> 00:00:06,234
section.

3
00:00:06,254 --> 00:00:08,020
Most students understand them.

4
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:12,054
They still lose points on them, because
these questions are built around a few

5
00:00:12,074 --> 00:00:14,110
very specific mistakes.

6
00:00:14,174 --> 00:00:16,189
Flipping a ratio upside down.

7
00:00:16,209 --> 00:00:17,832
Mixing minutes and hours.

8
00:00:17,852 --> 00:00:21,510
Converting square feet to square
yards by dividing by three.

9
00:00:21,530 --> 00:00:25,483
And reading a part-to-part ratio
as a fraction of the whole.

10
00:00:25,503 --> 00:00:28,946
In this lesson, you'll learn one
method that handles all of them:

11
00:00:28,966 --> 00:00:31,483
keep the units attached to every number,

12
00:00:31,503 --> 00:00:32,966
and let them cancel.

13
00:00:33,182 --> 00:00:36,609
Six practice questions,
getting harder as we go.

14
00:00:36,652 --> 00:00:38,330
Start with the vocabulary.

15
00:00:38,651 --> 00:00:43,937
A ratio compares two quantities, like
four sopranos for every seven altos.

16
00:00:44,079 --> 00:00:46,524
A rate is a ratio between
two different units,

17
00:00:46,544 --> 00:00:49,008
like miles per hour or dollars per pound.

18
00:00:49,089 --> 00:00:51,890
A unit rate tells you how much for one.

19
00:00:51,910 --> 00:00:54,890
If twelve pounds of apples
cost eighteen dollars,

20
00:00:54,910 --> 00:00:58,232
the unit rate is one dollar
and fifty cents per pound.

21
00:00:58,410 --> 00:01:00,696
Divide by the thing you want one of.

22
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:02,493
Some rates have special names.

23
00:01:02,513 --> 00:01:04,707
Speed is distance per time.

24
00:01:04,727 --> 00:01:09,564
Density is mass per volume, or people
per area for population density.

25
00:01:09,584 --> 00:01:13,707
A block with a mass of three hundred
grams and a volume of four hundred cubic

26
00:01:13,727 --> 00:01:18,977
centimeters has a density of zero point
seven five grams per cubic centimeter.

27
00:01:19,009 --> 00:01:22,488
Two quantities are proportional
when their ratio stays the same.

28
00:01:22,508 --> 00:01:25,739
That gives you the key fact:
if one quantity triples,

29
00:01:25,759 --> 00:01:27,238
the other triples too.

30
00:01:27,258 --> 00:01:29,560
A proportion is just two equal ratios,

31
00:01:29,580 --> 00:01:32,080
and you can solve it by cross multiplying.

32
00:01:32,109 --> 00:01:35,930
The College Board's description of
this skill lists the question types.

33
00:01:36,037 --> 00:01:37,966
Proportions and ratios.

34
00:01:38,073 --> 00:01:39,053
Rates.

35
00:01:39,073 --> 00:01:41,839
Unit conversions, both
one step and multistep.

36
00:01:41,859 --> 00:01:44,588
Derived units, like population
per square kilometer.

37
00:01:44,608 --> 00:01:46,002
And scale drawings.

38
00:01:46,031 --> 00:01:48,404
Every one of those comes
down to the same move.

39
00:01:48,424 --> 00:01:52,475
Write the units next to the numbers,
and set things up so the units you don't

40
00:01:52,495 --> 00:01:53,761
want cancel out.

41
00:01:53,781 --> 00:01:55,399
Let's start with proportions.

42
00:01:55,419 --> 00:01:56,471
Question one.

43
00:01:56,491 --> 00:02:00,169
A recipe uses three cups of
flour to make eight muffins.

44
00:02:00,205 --> 00:02:04,597
At this rate, how many cups of flour
are needed to make twenty muffins?

45
00:02:04,629 --> 00:02:05,843
Pause and try it.

46
00:02:09,089 --> 00:02:11,104
Set up the proportion with labels.

47
00:02:11,124 --> 00:02:13,962
Flour over muffins equals
flour over muffins.

48
00:02:13,982 --> 00:02:16,605
Three over eight equals x over twenty.

49
00:02:16,625 --> 00:02:18,748
Same units on top, same
units on the bottom.

50
00:02:18,768 --> 00:02:19,905
That's the whole rule.

51
00:02:19,925 --> 00:02:21,298
Cross multiply.

52
00:02:21,318 --> 00:02:25,012
Eight x equals sixty, so
x equals seven point five.

53
00:02:25,032 --> 00:02:26,512
The answer is B.

54
00:02:26,532 --> 00:02:29,905
Quick check: twenty muffins
is two and a half batches,

55
00:02:29,925 --> 00:02:33,103
and two and a half times three
cups is seven point five.

56
00:02:33,174 --> 00:02:35,581
Each wrong choice is a classic mistake.

57
00:02:35,601 --> 00:02:37,797
One hundred sixty thirds flips one ratio,

58
00:02:37,817 --> 00:02:40,475
so muffins end up on top on one side.

59
00:02:40,495 --> 00:02:43,725
Fifteen adds instead of
multiplying: twelve more muffins,

60
00:02:43,745 --> 00:02:45,225
so twelve more cups.

61
00:02:45,245 --> 00:02:47,439
And two point five is the scale factor,

62
00:02:47,459 --> 00:02:48,638
one step early.

63
00:02:48,693 --> 00:02:49,780
Question two.

64
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:54,265
In a choir, the ratio of sopranos
to altos is four to seven.

65
00:02:54,408 --> 00:02:58,602
The choir has seventy-seven members, and
each member is either a soprano or an

66
00:02:58,622 --> 00:02:59,458
alto.

67
00:02:59,478 --> 00:03:01,684
How many sopranos are in the choir?

68
00:03:01,704 --> 00:03:02,919
Pause and try it.

69
00:03:06,165 --> 00:03:09,002
Four to seven compares one
part to the other part.

70
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:10,288
It's part to part.

71
00:03:10,308 --> 00:03:13,358
It does not say four sevenths
of the choir are sopranos.

72
00:03:13,378 --> 00:03:15,215
To get the whole, add the parts.

73
00:03:15,235 --> 00:03:17,236
Four plus seven is eleven.

74
00:03:17,307 --> 00:03:20,271
So sopranos are four
elevenths of the choir.

75
00:03:20,306 --> 00:03:23,966
Seventy-seven divided by eleven
is seven members per part.

76
00:03:23,986 --> 00:03:29,073
Four parts is twenty-eight sopranos,
and seven parts is forty-nine altos.

77
00:03:29,093 --> 00:03:30,700
The answer is A.

78
00:03:30,735 --> 00:03:31,750
Forty-four is the trap.

79
00:03:31,770 --> 00:03:36,270
It's four sevenths of seventy-seven,
which treats the ratio as part to whole.

80
00:03:36,377 --> 00:03:38,341
Forty-nine is the altos.

81
00:03:38,377 --> 00:03:41,357
Thirty-three is seventy-seven
minus forty-four,

82
00:03:41,377 --> 00:03:43,214
the same mistake one step later.

83
00:03:43,234 --> 00:03:47,552
Check: twenty-eight to forty-nine
reduces to four to seven.

84
00:03:47,572 --> 00:03:49,322
Now unit conversions.

85
00:03:49,358 --> 00:03:52,017
The method is called dimensional analysis.

86
00:03:52,037 --> 00:03:55,088
Write each conversion as
a fraction equal to one,

87
00:03:55,108 --> 00:03:57,695
like sixty minutes over one hour.

88
00:03:57,715 --> 00:04:03,302
Then line the fractions up so each unit
you don't want appears once on top and

89
00:04:03,322 --> 00:04:04,488
once on the bottom.

90
00:04:04,508 --> 00:04:05,559
Question three.

91
00:04:05,579 --> 00:04:09,345
A pump removes water from a flooded
basement at a constant rate of two hundred

92
00:04:09,365 --> 00:04:11,059
fifty liters per minute.

93
00:04:11,079 --> 00:04:14,043
What is this rate in
cubic meters per hour?

94
00:04:14,186 --> 00:04:17,088
One cubic meter equals
one thousand liters.

95
00:04:17,108 --> 00:04:18,322
Pause and try it.

96
00:04:22,568 --> 00:04:24,798
Start with two hundred
fifty liters per minute.

97
00:04:24,818 --> 00:04:28,798
Minutes are on the bottom, so multiply
by sixty minutes over one hour.

98
00:04:28,818 --> 00:04:31,854
The minutes cancel, and
now it's liters per hour.

99
00:04:31,919 --> 00:04:36,526
Liters are on top, so multiply by one
cubic meter over one thousand liters.

100
00:04:36,669 --> 00:04:38,062
The liters cancel.

101
00:04:38,169 --> 00:04:40,955
What's left is cubic meters per hour.

102
00:04:41,026 --> 00:04:44,469
Two hundred fifty times sixty,
divided by one thousand,

103
00:04:44,489 --> 00:04:45,632
is fifteen.

104
00:04:45,811 --> 00:04:47,178
Enter fifteen.

105
00:04:47,198 --> 00:04:49,677
If you got fifteen thousand,
you skipped the liters.

106
00:04:49,697 --> 00:04:52,928
If you got zero point two
five, you skipped the minutes.

107
00:04:52,948 --> 00:04:55,768
A unit left over in the
wrong place is your warning.

108
00:04:55,804 --> 00:04:56,641
Question four.

109
00:04:56,661 --> 00:05:00,070
Machine A packs two hundred
seventy boxes per hour.

110
00:05:00,090 --> 00:05:03,054
Machine B packs six boxes per minute.

111
00:05:03,126 --> 00:05:05,427
Working at the same time at these rates,

112
00:05:05,447 --> 00:05:09,376
how many boxes do the two
machines pack in forty minutes?

113
00:05:09,452 --> 00:05:10,666
Pause and try it.

114
00:05:14,912 --> 00:05:16,249
The rates are in different units.

115
00:05:16,269 --> 00:05:18,642
One is per hour, and one is per minute.

116
00:05:18,662 --> 00:05:21,464
Before you add anything,
put them in the same unit.

117
00:05:21,484 --> 00:05:24,320
Two hundred seventy per
hour, divided by sixty,

118
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:26,519
is four point five boxes per minute.

119
00:05:26,583 --> 00:05:29,349
Together, they pack four
point five plus six,

120
00:05:29,369 --> 00:05:31,583
or ten point five boxes per minute.

121
00:05:31,797 --> 00:05:34,349
Rates for machines working
at the same time add.

122
00:05:34,369 --> 00:05:37,670
Ten point five times forty
minutes is four hundred twenty.

123
00:05:37,690 --> 00:05:39,218
The answer is C.

124
00:05:39,238 --> 00:05:41,182
Eleven thousand forty is the trap.

125
00:05:41,202 --> 00:05:44,753
It adds two hundred seventy and
six as if they were the same unit,

126
00:05:44,773 --> 00:05:46,574
then multiplies by forty.

127
00:05:46,594 --> 00:05:50,575
One hundred eighty-four converts
the time but not machine B's rate.

128
00:05:50,595 --> 00:05:53,475
And two hundred forty is machine B alone.

129
00:05:53,495 --> 00:05:55,475
Now the biggest trap in this skill.

130
00:05:55,495 --> 00:05:57,297
One yard is three feet.

131
00:05:57,317 --> 00:06:00,297
But one square yard is
not three square feet.

132
00:06:00,317 --> 00:06:02,760
A square yard is three feet by three feet,

133
00:06:02,780 --> 00:06:04,368
which is nine square feet.

134
00:06:04,388 --> 00:06:06,618
A cubic yard is three by three by three,

135
00:06:06,638 --> 00:06:08,524
which is twenty-seven cubic feet.

136
00:06:08,544 --> 00:06:11,794
So for area, square the conversion factor.

137
00:06:11,936 --> 00:06:14,009
For volume, cube it.

138
00:06:14,473 --> 00:06:16,774
Or convert the lengths
before you multiply,

139
00:06:16,794 --> 00:06:18,866
which avoids the problem completely.

140
00:06:18,891 --> 00:06:20,050
Question five.

141
00:06:20,070 --> 00:06:24,105
A rectangular floor measures
eighteen feet by twenty-four feet.

142
00:06:24,248 --> 00:06:27,085
Carpet costs thirty
dollars per square yard.

143
00:06:27,105 --> 00:06:30,463
What is the cost of carpet
to cover the entire floor?

144
00:06:30,497 --> 00:06:32,676
One yard equals three feet.

145
00:06:32,768 --> 00:06:33,982
Pause and try it.

146
00:06:38,228 --> 00:06:39,887
Convert the lengths first.

147
00:06:39,907 --> 00:06:44,228
Eighteen feet is six yards, and
twenty-four feet is eight yards.

148
00:06:44,442 --> 00:06:48,549
So the floor is six times eight,
or forty-eight square yards.

149
00:06:48,585 --> 00:06:52,672
At thirty dollars per square yard,
that's one thousand four hundred forty

150
00:06:52,692 --> 00:06:53,422
dollars.

151
00:06:53,442 --> 00:06:55,149
The answer is B.

152
00:06:55,169 --> 00:06:56,328
Check it the other way.

153
00:06:56,348 --> 00:06:59,578
The area is four hundred
thirty-two square feet.

154
00:06:59,598 --> 00:07:03,562
Divide by nine, not three,
and you get forty-eight again.

155
00:07:03,991 --> 00:07:06,276
Dividing by three gives choice C.

156
00:07:06,454 --> 00:07:09,113
Dividing by twenty-seven,
the cubic factor,

157
00:07:09,133 --> 00:07:09,471
gives A.

158
00:07:09,491 --> 00:07:12,483
And never converting at all gives D.

159
00:07:12,503 --> 00:07:14,733
Question six, the hardest one.

160
00:07:14,753 --> 00:07:18,269
On a map, one centimeter
represents five kilometers.

161
00:07:18,289 --> 00:07:22,446
A region shown on the map is a rectangle
that measures four centimeters by three

162
00:07:22,466 --> 00:07:23,466
centimeters.

163
00:07:23,502 --> 00:07:27,081
The region has a population
of forty-two thousand people.

164
00:07:27,101 --> 00:07:29,851
What is the population
density of the region,

165
00:07:30,173 --> 00:07:32,494
in people per square kilometer?

166
00:07:32,523 --> 00:07:33,610
Pause and try it.

167
00:07:33,630 --> 00:07:35,201
Take a little longer on this one.

168
00:07:39,387 --> 00:07:42,117
Population density is
people per square kilometer,

169
00:07:42,137 --> 00:07:43,974
so you need the real area.

170
00:07:43,994 --> 00:07:46,367
Don't scale the map's area by five.

171
00:07:46,387 --> 00:07:47,581
Scale the lengths.

172
00:07:47,601 --> 00:07:49,616
Four centimeters is twenty kilometers,

173
00:07:49,636 --> 00:07:52,387
and three centimeters
is fifteen kilometers.

174
00:07:52,422 --> 00:07:54,794
So the real area is twenty times fifteen,

175
00:07:54,814 --> 00:07:56,902
or three hundred square kilometers.

176
00:07:56,922 --> 00:08:01,008
Forty-two thousand people divided by
three hundred square kilometers is one

177
00:08:01,028 --> 00:08:03,437
hundred forty people per square kilometer.

178
00:08:03,457 --> 00:08:05,360
Enter one hundred forty.

179
00:08:05,380 --> 00:08:06,416
Here's the trap.

180
00:08:06,559 --> 00:08:09,289
The map area is twelve square centimeters,

181
00:08:09,309 --> 00:08:11,467
and twelve times five is sixty.

182
00:08:11,487 --> 00:08:13,538
That gives a density of seven hundred,

183
00:08:13,558 --> 00:08:15,503
five times too big.

184
00:08:15,523 --> 00:08:19,360
Each square centimeter on this
map is five by five kilometers,

185
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:21,737
which is twenty-five square kilometers.

186
00:08:21,786 --> 00:08:23,500
Here's the test-day method.

187
00:08:23,820 --> 00:08:28,266
Step one: write the units next
to every number in the question,

188
00:08:28,286 --> 00:08:30,551
including the units the answer needs.

189
00:08:30,571 --> 00:08:33,393
That tells you where you're
going before you start.

190
00:08:33,442 --> 00:08:36,814
Step two: for ratios, ask part to part,

191
00:08:36,834 --> 00:08:38,208
or part to whole.

192
00:08:38,228 --> 00:08:41,244
If it's part to part, add
the parts to get the whole.

193
00:08:41,264 --> 00:08:45,651
For proportions, keep the same units on
top and the same units on the bottom.

194
00:08:45,671 --> 00:08:50,544
Step three: for conversions, chain fractions
so the units you don't want cancel.

195
00:08:50,564 --> 00:08:52,757
For area, square the factor.

196
00:08:52,777 --> 00:08:54,564
For volume, cube it.

197
00:08:54,599 --> 00:08:56,528
Or convert the lengths first.

198
00:08:56,561 --> 00:08:58,740
Step four: sense check.

199
00:08:58,954 --> 00:09:01,649
A bigger unit on top
means a smaller number:

200
00:09:01,669 --> 00:09:05,418
fifteen cubic meters per
hour, not fifteen thousand.

201
00:09:05,489 --> 00:09:08,597
A bigger unit on the bottom
means a bigger number:

202
00:09:08,668 --> 00:09:12,979
two hundred fifty liters per minute
is fifteen thousand liters per hour.

203
00:09:12,999 --> 00:09:16,392
If the size looks wrong,
a unit didn't cancel.

204
00:09:16,429 --> 00:09:17,338
Quick recap.

205
00:09:17,358 --> 00:09:19,481
A rate is a ratio with units.

206
00:09:19,501 --> 00:09:22,409
Keep the units on every
number and let them cancel.

207
00:09:22,429 --> 00:09:26,143
A part-to-part ratio needs the
parts added to get the whole.

208
00:09:26,179 --> 00:09:28,338
Rates for things working together add,

209
00:09:28,358 --> 00:09:29,695
once they share a unit.

210
00:09:29,715 --> 00:09:33,536
And square or cube the
factor for area and volume.

211
00:09:33,559 --> 00:09:38,646
Every question here was written for this
video in the style of the real test.

212
00:09:38,666 --> 00:09:43,146
For official practice, the College Board's
free Question Bank lets you filter by

213
00:09:43,166 --> 00:09:47,396
skill, including ratios, rates,
proportional relationships,

214
00:09:47,416 --> 00:09:48,702
and units.

215
00:09:48,770 --> 00:09:50,500
If this helped, subscribe.

216
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:54,500
The next video is SAT
probability and two-way tables,

217
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:57,306
where picking the right
total is the whole game.
